{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>In the place where … is slaughtered, etc.</b> On the corner of the altar in the north. And what does this teach? For was it not already stated in the law of the guilt-offering, in the section of ״צַו אֶת אַהֲרֹן״, that the guilt-offering requires slaughter in the north? Because this one departed from the category of guilt-offerings to be judged by the law of waving — one might say its slaughter should be in the place of its waving; therefore it is stated ״וְשָׁחַט … בִּמְקוֹם אֲשֶׁר יִשְׁחַט וְגוֹ׳״ (Sifra)." "<b>For like the sin-offering.</b> For like all sin-offerings <b>this guilt-offering</b> <b>is for the priest</b> — in all services that depend on the priest, this guilt-offering was equated to the sin-offering. That you should not say: since its blood departed from the category of the rest of the guilt-offerings, to be applied on the thumb and the toes, it should not require placing of blood and emurim toward the altar — therefore it is stated ״כִּי כַחַטָּאת הָאָשָׁם הוּא לַכֹּהֵן״. One might say its blood should be placed above, like the sin-offering — Scripture teaches, etc., in Torat Kohanim."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:06:27.594657733Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}